# Commit identity

For **every** `git commit` in this repository (including amend when allowed), set the author explicitly:

```bash
git commit --author="saroj990 <saroj990@github.com>" -m "..."
```

Do not rely on the machine’s auto-detected name/email. If a commit was created without this author, fix with `git commit --amend --reset-author --author="saroj990 <saroj990@github.com>"` only when amend rules allow.
